        "abstract": "A strain-balanced InGaAs/GaAs pin multiple quantum well modulator has been constructed and demonstrated to have a modulation contrast ratio of 1.74:1 in transmission. The quantum efficiency of the device when used as a detector was approximately 99%, even without the application of an external bias. Simulations show that if the device is configured as an S-SEED and an epitaxial mirror is incorporated, bistable operation with 2V supply voltage threshold and a reasonable contrast ratio can be obtained in the 1040 nm region.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
